new details are emerging this morning in  connection with a string of unexplained  shootings at a popular campsite along  southern california's malibu coast  police are now considering a possible  link between last week's deadly attack  on a man while he was sleeping and seven  other unsolved shootings Carter Evans  reports investigators still aren't  talking a week after the fatal shooting  of a father camping at Malibu Creek  State Park detectives were back looking  for evidence tristan Beaudette was  killed while sleeping in a tent with his  daughters ages 2 and 4 according to the  LA Times he was shot in the head  although there is no known motive for  the killing homicide detectives  confirmed seven other shootings in the  area dating back to November 2016  these are shotgun pellets  yeah it's bird shots James Rodgers was  shot in the arm while sleeping at a  campsite nearby I think there should  have an officer staked out here to be  honest at night since most of these  attacks have come at night  Rodgers doesn't feel safe here anymore  and he believes the shooter may have  been aiming to kill him I kind of  assumed they were aiming for my head to  be honest others are now speaking out  the owner of this Tesla says his car was  shot while he was driving near the park  at around 4:00 in the morning just four  days before Beaudette was killed and  Melissa tangelo had a similar experience  while she was camping in her SUV they  all say they feel like their reports  weren't taken seriously the Sheriff's  Department is not responded to our  repeated requests for an interview but  on Friday released a statement saying a  link between the past shootings and the  murder will be explored the park  stretches over more than 12 square miles  in the Santa Monica Mountains and while  the campground is closed indefinitely  the park remains open to hikers and  families looking for a spot to cool off  there are warnings posted here for  everything from rattlesnakes to poison  oak but there's nothing about the  shootings and that's unacceptable to  many park visitors there was a family  from Maryland who just came by they  didn't know that there was a killing  down here and he could be out here but  there's no warnings or anything posted  up it's just you kind of have to find  out on your own you know for CBS this  morning Saturday Carter Evans Calabasas  California
 

